      <div type="clause" n="54.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 54.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hine mon gilt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.3-3"/>, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> mot he gesellan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.4-3"/> on þara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.5-2"/> hyndenna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.6-2"/> gehwelcere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.7-2"/> monnan ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.8"/> byrnan ⁊ sweord on þæt wergild<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.9"/>, gif he ðyrfe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.10"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hine man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.2-2"/> gylt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/>, ðonne mot he gesyllan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/> án þara<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.3-2"/> hyndena<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.4-2"/> gehwylcere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.5"/> monna<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.6"/> byrnan ⁊ sweord on ðæt wergild, gif he ðurfe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="114" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf hine mon gylt, ðonne mot he gesyllan on ðæra hyndenna gehwylcre monnan ⁊ byrnan ⁊ sweord on þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> wergyld, gyf he ðurfe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="54.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="115" ed="#liebermann"/>Si reddatur, tunc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.1"/> licebit dari<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.2"/> in illa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.3"/> societate quorumcumque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.4"/> hominum loricam et gladium, si opus sit, in weregildo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="54" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif hine mon gilt, þonne mot he gesellan on þara hyndenna gehwelcere monnan<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#Ine_54-1.attnote.fn.13"/> ⁊ byrnan ⁊ sweord, on þæt wergild, gif he ðyrfe.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="57.1" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="418" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Gif hine mon gilt, þon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi> mot he gesellan on þara hyndenna gehwelcere monnan ⁊ byrnan ⁊ sweord on þæt wergild, gif he ðyrfe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="115" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn man diesen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.de.1"/> entgilt, dann darf man auf dies Wergeld, wenn man [durch Armuth<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.de.2"/>] muss, in<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.de.3"/> jeder<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.de.4"/> der Hundertzahlen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.de.5"/> [der Schillingsumme des Wergelds je] einen Sklaven<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.de.6"/> und einen Panzer und ein Schwert<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_54-1.lnote.de.7"/> einzahlen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If one pays for this man, then one may, if one has to [through poverty], pay into this wergeld in each of the hundreds [of the shilling-sum of the wergeld] a slave and a coat of mail and a sword [each].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="55" ed="#attenborough"/>If payment is made for the dead man, then he [the slayer] may, if need be<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_54-1.attnote.n.1"/>, include a man<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_54-1.attnote.n.2"/> [i.e. a slave] and<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_54-1.attnote.n.3"/> a coat of mail, and<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_54-1.attnote.n.3"/> a sword<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_54-1.attnote.n.4"/>, in each hundred shillings of the wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="406" ed="#whitelock"/>And if wergild is paid, then he may give in each of the hundreds [of the wergild] a slave, and a coat-of-mail and a sword, if he need.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="419" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If recompense is made for [the slain man], then he may include in each hundred [shillings] a man [=slave] and a byrnie and a sword towards the wergild, if he needs to.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="419"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Af_18-1">Af 18.1</ref> <quote>Alfred §21 requires a fine paid in livestock, but specifically prohibits the substitution of a slave.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="419"><label>see</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_32">Ine 32</ref> <quote>The value of a Welsh slave was 50 shillings (see §32 and note)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="313"><ref target="clause:Af_18-1">Af 18.1</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus Lond; fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from Lond; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">dare <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">dare MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. i. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. i. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">115</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quibuscumque hominibus <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quibuscumque hominibus Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> þæra</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to þæra</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> -enna</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to -enna</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">zweites</hi> e <hi rend="italic">übergeschr., letztes</hi> e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">second e written above, last e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Punkt dahinter</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">point after it</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gylt <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gylt So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.4-3" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesyl. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesyl. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæra <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæra So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ena <hi rend="italic">So Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ena So Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gehwylcre <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gehwylcre Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wærgyld <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> wergyld <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wærgyld So; wergyld Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">114</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðurfe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðurfe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘ihn schuldig findet’, eine Bed., die <hi rend="italic">gyltan</hi>, woran Frühere aus H B So denken, nicht hat. Q leitet richtig von <hi rend="italic">gieldan</hi> ab</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘finds him guilty’, a meaning which <hi rend="italic">gyltan</hi>, which earlier scholars have in mind on the basis of H B So, does not have. Q rightly derives it from <hi rend="italic">gieldan</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Wergeld 20; Waffen 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Wergeld 20; Waffen 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘an’ Frühere; allein ‘jemandem geben’ heisst <hi rend="italic">sellan</hi> m. blossem Dativ</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘on’ earlier scholars; but ‘to give to someone’ is <hi rend="italic">sellan</hi> with the simple dative</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Als Plural versteht <hi rend="italic">gehwylcre</hi> Q, was für Ines Zeit nicht angeht</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q takes <hi rend="italic">gehwylcre</hi> as a plural, which is not possible for Ine’s time</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> 54⁸</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 54⁸</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Männer-Panzer’ kann H’s Meinung nicht sein, weil Interpunktion dazwischen steht; vielleicht ‘an (von) Sklaven’? Auch Q las diesen gen. plur. Dass Sklaven allerdings zur Busszahlung dienten, <hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Af 18, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Men’s coats of mail’ cannot be H’s meaning, because there is punctuation between the words; perhaps ‘in (of) slaves’? Q too read this gen. plur. That slaves were, however, used in paying compensation, <hi rend="italic">see</hi> Af 18, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_54-1.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">78</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Da ein Unfreier (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7 a) 60 Schill., Panzer (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi>) und Schwert (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 4) ebenfalls viel gilt, sind die 3 Stücke zusammen 100 volle Schilling wert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Since an unfree man (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7 a) is worth 60 shill., and a coat of mail (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi>) and a sword (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 4) are likewise worth a great deal, the 3 items together are worth a full 100 shillings</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_54-1.attnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">54</biblScope></bibl><label>monnan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">monna</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_54-1.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘if he need’ that is to say, if he has not the value at hand, in money or other articles.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_54-1.attnote.n.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The value of the slave in Wessex was 60 shillings (cf. note 3 to Ine, cap. 23 § 3); a mailcoat and sword together would probably be worth quite 40.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_54-1.attnote.n.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Or possibly ‘or’; see the following note.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_54-1.attnote.n.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">191</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Swords were sometimes worth much more than this, see Harmer, <hi rend="italic">Historical Documents</hi>, p. 4: <hi rend="italic">Freoðomund foe to minum sweorde ⁊ agefe ðeræt feower ðusenda, ⁊ him mon forgefe ðeran ðreotene hund pending</hi>; and Thorpe, <hi rend="italic">Diplomatarium Anglicum</hi> (<hi rend="italic">Will of the Atheling Æthelstan</hi>). For the value of arms etc. in later times, see II Can. cap. 71 f.</seg></note>
      </div>
